<title>JAPAN: Honda shares up on bargain hunting.</title>
<headline>Honda shares up on bargain hunting.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Honda Motor Co Ltd rose on Monday morning on bargain-hunting after declining for seven consecutive trading days on the Tokyo Stock Exchange, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were up 110 yen at 3,410 yen at 0056 GMT.  </p>
<p>&quot;Shares in Honda are rising on bargain-hunting since falling about 20 percent after hitting their lifetime high of 4,180 yen on May 8,&quot; said a trader.</p>
</text>
